%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:unknown -- a name without a NED type stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code needs a NED type for the name (TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm()).

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms.

Host under test: host1, whose connection creates its algorithm at the open. Observation: the
error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: unknown
%# value: "NoSuchTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassUnknown compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "NoSuchTcp"    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
The TCP algorithm "NoSuchTcp" has no NED type
